fidelity report — BPMN 2.0
  [P-DMNWIRED] advisory — Split_0
      The gateway's arms are decided by the DMN decision ‘ongoing reporting obligation’ (id decision_ongoing_reporting_obligation) in model ‘SEC Regulation Crowdfunding — 17 CFR Part 227’, invoked by the businessRuleTask in front of it; each outgoing flow now tests that decision's answer (verdict shape) rather than restating the L4 guard, which moves to the flow's <documentation>.
      lost: nothing an engine needs, but the arms' exhaustiveness and mutual exclusion are now properties of the DMN table's hit policy rather than of this gateway, and BPMN still has no way to say so here
  [F1] blocking — Task_1
      MUST, MAY and SHANT all draw as a task, so nothing here makes skipping this one a breach and skipping another one fine.
      lost: the deontic modality, which survives in the label and the <documentation> but has no notational force
  [P-DEADLINE] blocking — Boundary_1
      Deadline ‘`business days to file Form C-TR`’ is not an ISO 8601 duration and no unit could be read from it, so the boundary event carries the text verbatim as a condition rather than a timer carrying a duration we invented.
      lost: the deadline as a machine-checkable timer
  [F1] blocking — Task_4
      MUST, MAY and SHANT all draw as a task, so nothing here makes skipping this one a breach and skipping another one fine.
      lost: the deontic modality, which survives in the label and the <documentation> but has no notational force
  [P-DEADLINE] blocking — Boundary_4
      Deadline ‘`days to file the annual report after fiscal year end`’ is not an ISO 8601 duration and no unit could be read from it, so the boundary event carries the text verbatim as a condition rather than a timer carrying a duration we invented.
      lost: the deadline as a machine-checkable timer
  [P-CYCLE] lossy — Process_ongoing_reporting_obligation
      The state graph has a cycle (initial, Issuer must file a Form C-AR annual report). BPMN can draw a loop, but this layout places a node by its longest path from the start and a node on a cycle has none, so inside the loop a node further right no longer means a moment further on: the positions are wherever the relaxation ran out of fuel.
      lost: the reading that left-to-right is time, which is the only thing the horizontal axis was carrying
  [F2] lossy — Process_ongoing_reporting_obligation
      A lane says who performs the work, where L4's PARTY says who owes the obligation, and this diagram can only show the first (lanes here: Issuer).
      lost: the bearer, as distinct from the performer — the two come apart whenever an agent acts for a principal
  [F5] advisory — Process_ongoing_reporting_obligation
      BPMN has no as-of date, so any threshold or deadline that does appear in this diagram is a value someone must remember to edit when the rule changes.
      lost: asking the same question as of a different rule date, which the L4 source can still answer
